{"chunk_id":"939181","wall_time_seconds":0.347922875,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":681,"output":"{"body":"## Why\n\nFunder pages should follow the MP layout, use the summary space for party and timeline charts, and offer a separate funding history view.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Put total funded on the right and a compact party pie beside a monthly funding timeline. Party amounts appear on hover, keyboard focus or tap. Legends with more than two parties use two columns.\n- Retain the top ten recipients and remove currency codes and explanatory currency text. Summary charts follow the MP page's GBP basis.\n- Add funding history with recipient links, registration date filters and pagination. Derive totals and history from the same source records.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis covers funder details and frontend summary charts. The MP and funder timelines share exact UTC calendar-month aggregation and rendering, with earnings category selection retained for MPs. Search behavior and database schema remain unchanged.\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\nThe existing endpoint returns complete history, matching the MP page. Summary totals use all recipients before the top ten limit. Negative and unavailable party totals remain accessible through party controls.\n\n## Blast Radius\n\nThe frontend requires the updated funder response, so the frontend and backend must be released together. The shared timeline preserves MP earnings selection, exact signed values, missing amounts and undated exclusions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All 53 frontend tests, Svelte check, production build and formatting passed. Tests cover pie hover, focus, touch and dismissal, exact monthly values, responsive layout and MP behavior.\n- Six isolated SQLx and HTTP detail tests, Rust compiler checks and formatting passed. Five frozen HTTP search and recorded-name regressions passed.\n- Live Unite totals reconcile 104 records with £618,900 and a £386,000 peak registration month. Both chart layouts and the visible tooltip were inspected. Google UK Ltd's four-party legend was checked on desktop and at 360px. Monthly tests cover timezone boundaries, year rollover, leap February, empty months and negative totals for both pages. Clippy remains blocked by seven existing declaration-loading and CLI diagnostics, with none in changed files.\n\n![Funding history with date filters and pagination](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56858e7f-1db9-4ec3-88ee-f1a88feb5dff)\n\n![Google UK Ltd party pie beside monthly funding timeline](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05af8a41-3862-4fb2-8375-82926188717d)\n\n![MP earnings timeline grouped by registration month](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/071a0dc1-2308-4047-ace3-ef9ccbba0839)","isDraft":false,"url":"https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/55"}
